      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIRC,volatile has been used with the download_from_flash implementation in our source code for some time. However, running a test where I removed the volatile keyword from all of the ROM functions and then exercised the ROM functions via console commands: \u0027reboot RO\u0027 which exercises download_from_flash and \u0027rollbackaddent\u0027 which exercises OTP APIs, I didn\u0027t see any negative side effects. To Caveh\u0027s point, the underlying code in ROM can\u0027t change per chip by definition, so I don\u0027t see a reason why volatile is needed",
